---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { withBase } from '../lib/url';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Terms and Conditions"
  description="The terms that govern your use of Mindtivate."
>
  <section class="section container prose-page">
    <p class="eyebrow">Legal</p>
    <h1>Terms and conditions</h1>
    <p><em>Last updated: August 2026.</em></p>

    <p>
      These terms govern your use of Mindtivate (this website). By using
      the site, you agree to them. If you don't agree, please don't use
      the site.
    </p>

    <h2>Not medical advice</h2>
    <p>
      Mindtivate publishes general health, fitness, and wellness
      information for educational purposes only. It is not medical advice,
      and it isn't a substitute for a diagnosis, treatment, or guidance
      from a qualified healthcare provider. Always talk to a doctor or
      other qualified provider before making changes based on anything you
      read here, especially if you have an existing condition or are
      pregnant, nursing, or managing a diagnosis.
    </p>

    <h2>Use of the site</h2>
    <p>
      You agree to use Mindtivate only for lawful purposes and not to
      misuse the site — for example, by attempting to disrupt it, scrape
      it at a harmful scale, submit spam through our forms, or interfere
      with other visitors' use of it.
    </p>

    <h2>Content and intellectual property</h2>
    <p>
      Articles, graphics, and other content on Mindtivate belong to
      Mindtivate or are used with permission, unless otherwise noted.
      You're welcome to link to our articles and quote brief excerpts with
      attribution and a link back to the original page. Republishing full
      articles or substantial portions without permission isn't allowed.
    </p>

    <h2>Affiliate links and third-party sites</h2>
    <p>
      Some links on Mindtivate are affiliate links, meaning we may earn a
      commission if you click through and make a purchase, at no extra
      cost to you — see our <a href={withBase('/affiliate-disclosure')}>affiliate disclosure</a> for details.
      Mindtivate isn't responsible for the content, accuracy, products, or
      privacy practices of any third-party site you reach through a link
      on this site.
    </p>

    <h2>No guarantees</h2>
    <p>
      We do our best to research and fact-check what we publish, but
      health research evolves, and we can't guarantee that every piece of
      content is complete, current, or error-free. The site and its
      content are provided "as is," without warranties of any kind.
    </p>

    <h2>Limitation of liability</h2>
    <p>
      To the fullest extent permitted by law, Mindtivate isn't liable for
      any damages or losses arising from your use of — or inability to
      use — this site or its content, including decisions you make based
      on it.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes to these terms</h2>
    <p>
      We may update these terms from time to time. Material changes will
      be reflected by updating the date at the top of this page. Continued
      use of the site after a change means you accept the updated terms.
    </p>

    <h2>Questions</h2>
    <p>
      If you have questions about these terms, <a href={withBase('/contact')}>contact us</a>.
    </p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .prose-page {
    max-width: 720px;
  }
</style>
